{"id":"ee11792e-6dc8-4390-abf7-a8b1fd62590c","revision":0,"last_node_id":32,"last_link_id":54,"nodes":[{"id":1,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[0,-440],"size":[3760,380],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["## Arbor · Camera angles by prompt — every character × every angle (Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo edit)\n\nTwo character pictures, eight camera angles written as plain instructions: Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo redraws each character from each angle (16 edits), and the **Compare Viewer** flips through them as *Mei · original*, *Mei · 3/4 left* … *Kai · wide*.\n\n1. **Characters** is a Load Media with one group per character (`# Mei`, `# Kai`): one branch each, named.\n2. **Angle names** and **Angle instructions** are two Panels in the same order — short names for the labels, full sentences for the model. **Prompt Template** (*zip*) adds *keep the same subject, clothes, colours, lighting and art style* to every instruction.\n3. **Cross Reference** pairs every character with every instruction, branch by branch: each character's branch holds its picture eight times and the eight instructions. Two **Tree to Data** give the edit model *image 1* and the prompt side by side.\n4. **Construct Tree** puts the edits back into one branch per character; **Merge** puts each original in front of its edits.\n5. **Collect** makes the labels — *original* plus the angle names — for the **Image Grid** columns and the **Compare Viewer** (*labels*: one list serves every character). **Save by Path** writes `output/arbor/angles/0 · Mei/back.png …`.\n\nWhat works best: turning the subject (3/4, profile, back), high / low / top-down shots, close-up and wide. Write the angle as a shot (\"Low-angle shot from near the floor…\") rather than \"move the camera\" — the model may draw a camera. Use your own pictures with **Add…** on Load Media; add an angle by adding a line to both panels."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## Arbor · Camera angles by prompt — every character × every angle (Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo edit)\n\nTwo character pictures, eight camera angles written as plain instructions: Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo redraws each character from each angle (16 edits), and the **Compare Viewer** flips through them as *Mei · original*, *Mei · 3/4 left* … *Kai · wide*.\n\n1. **Characters** is a Load Media with one group per character (`# Mei`, `# Kai`): one branch each, named.\n2. **Angle names** and **Angle instructions** are two Panels in the same order — short names for the labels, full sentences for the model. **Prompt Template** (*zip*) adds *keep the same subject, clothes, colours, lighting and art style* to every instruction.\n3. **Cross Reference** pairs every character with every instruction, branch by branch: each character's branch holds its picture eight times and the eight instructions. Two **Tree to Data** give the edit model *image 1* and the prompt side by side.\n4. **Construct Tree** puts the edits back into one branch per character; **Merge** puts each original in front of its edits.\n5. **Collect** makes the labels — *original* plus the angle names — for the **Image Grid** columns and the **Compare Viewer** (*labels*: one list serves every character). **Save by Path** writes `output/arbor/angles/0 · Mei/back.png …`.\n\nWhat works best: turning the subject (3/4, profile, back), high / low / top-down shots, close-up and wide. Write the angle as a shot (\"Low-angle shot from near the floor…\") rather than \"move the camera\" — the model may draw a camera. Use your own pictures with **Add…** on Load Media; add an angle by adding a line to both panels."},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":2,"type":"Arbor_LoadMedia","pos":[0,0],"size":[420,363],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"文件","name":"files","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"files"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"文件","name":"files","type":"ARBOR_TREE","links":[]},{"localized_name":"图片","name":"images","type":"ARBOR_TREE","li